# ~/.gitignore — whitelist dotfiles (repo rooted at $HOME).
# Strategy per rgbcu.be/blog/gitignore: ignore everything, then re-include by name.
# Nothing is tracked unless a line below explicitly allows it, so credentials and
# machine state can never sneak in. Directory must be un-ignored before its contents.

# --- ignore all ---
*

# --- meta ---
!.gitignore
!.gitmodules

# --- home rc ---
# Migrated to home-manager: ~/.bashrc, ~/.profile, ~/.tmux.conf and git config are
# now deployed as /nix/store symlinks by nixos-config (home/ layer stack). They are
# no longer tracked here — the flake is their single source of truth.

# --- submodules (own repos; gitlinks only, contents managed by the submodule) ---
!nixos-config
!.config/
!.config/nvim
# darwin: Matei3dMac platform configs — separate repo so it clones/pins independently
!darwin

# --- ~/.config, per tool ---
# btop, nix and nushell configs are home-manager-managed now (see nixos-config's
# home/common.nix and home/linux.nix); left ignored so their store symlinks and
# *.hm-bak backups don't get tracked. Add new per-tool entries here only for
# configs NOT owned by home-manager.

# --- ~/.claude: config only; secrets/transcripts/caches stay ignored by `*` ---
!.claude/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
!.claude/themes/
!.claude/themes/**
!.claude/settings.json